scalar-fields-for-filtering--display","content":"🗂️ Scalar Fields: For Filtering & Display","locale":"en"},"1709":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#-vector-embeddings-for-semantic-relevance","content":"📐 Vector Embeddings: For Semantic Relevance","locale":"en"},"1710":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#create-and-open-a-collection","content":"To create a new collection in Zvec, you need to define the following:","locale":"en"},"1711":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#create-and-open-a-collection","content":"**Schema** —  the structural blueprint of your data, specifying scalar fields and vector embeddings.","locale":"en"},"1712":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#create-and-open-a-collection","content":"**Collection options** (optional) — runtime settings that control how the collection behaves when opened (e.g., read-only mode).","locale":"en"},"1713":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#create-and-open-a-collection","content":"Once defined, call `create_and_open()` to initialize a new collection at a specified path and return a `Collection` object ready for inserts and queries.","locale":"en"},"1714":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#create-and-open-a-collection","content":"If a collection already exists at the specified path, `create_and_open()` will raise an error to prevent accidental overwrites.","locale":"en"},"1715":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#create-and-open-a-collection","content":"<Card icon=\"<TableOfContents className=&#x22;text-fd-primary&#x22; />\" title=\"Schema\" href=\"./schema/\" />","locale":"en"},"1716":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#create-and-open-a-collection","content":"<Card icon=\"<Settings className=&#x22;text-fd-primary&#x22; />\" title=\"Collection Options\" href=\"./options/\" />","locale":"en"},"1717":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#real-world-example--product-search","content":"This schema models a **multi-modal product search system**, combining visual, textual, and structured metadata for rich retrieval:","locale":"en"},"1718":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#️-scalar-fields-for-filtering--display","content":"`category` (array of strings, indexed): Enables queries like `category CONTAIN_ANY (\"electronics\", \"headphones\")` to find products that belong to either \"electronics\" or \"headphones\" (or both).","locale":"en"},"1719":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#️-scalar-fields-for-filtering--display","content":"`price` (integer, indexed with range optimization): Supports fast range queries such as `price > 100`.","locale":"en"},"1720":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#️-scalar-fields-for-filtering--display","content":"`in_stock` (boolean, indexed): Enables instant filtering by availability (e.g., \"only show items in stock\").","locale":"en"},"1721":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#️-scalar-fields-for-filtering--display","content":"`image_url` and `description` are stored but **not indexed**, since they're only used for display.","locale":"en"},"1722":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#-vector-embeddings-for-semantic-relevance","content":"Two dense vectors capture semantic meaning:","locale":"en"},"1723":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#-vector-embeddings-for-semantic-relevance","content":"`image_vec`: 512-dimensional embeddings from product images (e.g., via a vision model).","locale":"en"},"1724":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#-vector-embeddings-for-semantic-relevance","content":"`description_vec`: 768-dimensional embeddings from product descriptions (e.g., from a language model), stored with quantization.","locale":"en"},"1725":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create#-vector-embeddings-for-semantic-relevance","content":"One sparse vector `keywords_sparse` for keyword matching, enabling hybrid sparse-dense search.","locale":"en"},"1726":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/options","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/options","type":"page","content":"Options","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Collections","Create"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/options","locale":"en"},"1727":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/options-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/options","content":"The `CollectionOption` lets you control runtime behavior when creating or opening a collection:","locale":"en"},"1728":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/options-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/options","content":"`read_only`: Opens the collection in read-only mode. Attempts to write will raise an error.","locale":"en"},"1729":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/options-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/options","content":"**Note**: `read_only` must be set to `False` when calling `create_and_open()`, since creation requires writing files to disk.","locale":"en"},"1730":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/options-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/options","content":"`enable_mmap`: Uses memory-mapped I/O for faster access (default to `True`). This trades slightly higher memory cache usage for improved performance.","locale":"en"},"1731":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","type":"page","content":"Schema","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Collections","Create"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","locale":"en"},"1732":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#collection-name-step","content":"Collection Name","locale":"en"},"1733":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#scalar-fields-step","content":"Scalar Fields","locale":"en"},"1734":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#vectors-embeddings-step","content":"Vectors (Embeddings)","locale":"en"},"1735":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#choosing-vector-index-type","content":"Choosing Vector Index Type","locale":"en"},"1736":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#full-schema-example","content":"Full Schema Example","locale":"en"},"1737":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","content":"A **collection schema** `CollectionSchema` defines the structure that every document inserted into the collection must conform to.","locale":"en"},"1738":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","content":"The schema in Zvec is **dynamic**: you can add or remove scalar fields and vectors at any time without rebuilding the collection.","locale":"en"},"1739":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","content":"`CollectionSchema` has three parts:","locale":"en"},"1740":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","content":"`name`: An identifier for the collection.","locale":"en"},"1741":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","content":"`fields`: A list of scalar fields.","locale":"en"},"1742":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","content":"`vectors`: A list of vector fields.","locale":"en"},"1743":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#collection-name-step","content":"A human-readable identifier for your collection. This name is used internally for reference and logging.","locale":"en"},"1744":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#scalar-fields-step","content":"Scalar fields store non-vector (i.e., structured) data — such as strings, numbers, booleans, or arrays.","locale":"en"},"1745":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#scalar-fields-step","content":"Each field is defined using `FieldSchema` with the following properties:","locale":"en"},"1746":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#scalar-fields-step","content":"`name`: A unique string identifier for the field within the collection.","locale":"en"},"1747":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#scalar-fields-step","content":"`data_type`: The type of data stored — e.g., `STRING`, `INT64`, or array types like `ARRAY_STRING`.","locale":"en"},"1748":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#scalar-fields-step","content":"`nullable` (optional): Whether the field is allowed to **have no value** (defaults to `False`).","locale":"en"},"1749":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#scalar-fields-step","content":"`index_param` (optional): Enables fast filtering via `InvertIndexParam` (inverted index) or full-text search via `FtsIndexParam` (full-text index).","locale":"en"},"1750":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#scalar-fields-step","content":"Add an index to fields you plan to filter on. Unindexed fields save storage and write overhead.","locale":"en"},"1751":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#scalar-fields-step","content":"For **inverted indexes** (`InvertIndexParam`), you can optionally activate performance-enhancing (but storage-costly) features:","locale":"en"},"1752":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#scalar-fields-step","content":"`enable_range_optimization=True` → faster range queries (e.g., `price > 100`)","locale":"en"},"1753":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#scalar-fields-step","content":"`enable_extended_wildcard=True` → complex string pattern matching (e.g., `name LIKE 'abc%def'`)","locale":"en"},"1754":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#scalar-fields-step","content":"For **full-text indexes** (`FtsIndexParam`), configure the tokenizer and token filters instead. See full-text search for details.","locale":"en"},"1755":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#scalar-fields-step","content":"Use `InvertIndexParam()` to configure an inverted index.","locale":"en"},"1756":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#scalar-fields-step","content":"Use `FtsIndexParam()` to configure a full-text index.","locale":"en"},"1757":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#vectors-embeddings-step","content":"A vector is defined using `VectorSchema` with the following properties:","locale":"en"},"1758":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#vectors-embeddings-step","content":"`name`: A unique string identifier for the vector within the collection.","locale":"en"},"1759":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#vectors-embeddings-step","content":"`data_type`: The numeric format of the vector.","locale":"en"},"1760":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#vectors-embeddings-step","content":"Dense vectors: `VECTOR_FP32`, `VECTOR_FP16`, etc.","locale":"en"},"1761":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#vectors-embeddings-step","content":"Sparse vectors: `SPARSE_VECTOR_FP32`, `SPARSE_VECTOR_FP16`.","locale":"en"},"1762":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#vectors-embeddings-step","content":"`dimension`: Required for dense vectors — the number of dimensions.","locale":"en"},"1763":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-31","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#vectors-embeddings-step","content":"`index_param`: Configures the vector index type and similarity metric.","locale":"en"},"1764":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-32","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#choosing-vector-index-type","content":"The `index_param` allows you to configure the appropriate indexing strategy:","locale":"en"},"1765":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-33","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#choosing-vector-index-type","content":"`metric_type`: `COSINE`, `L2`, or `IP` (inner product) — &#x2A;Ensure your metric matches how your embeddings were trained!*","locale":"en"},"1766":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-34","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#choosing-vector-index-type","content":"`quantize_type` (optional): Compress vectors to reduce index size and speed up search (with slight recall trade-off).","locale":"en"},"1767":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-35","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#choosing-vector-index-type","content":"`quantizer_param` (optional): Additional quantizer parameters, e.g. `enable_rotate` (reduces quantization recall loss via random rotation).","locale":"en"},"1768":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-36","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#choosing-vector-index-type","content":"Use `FlatIndexParam()` to configure a Flat index.","locale":"en"},"1769":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-37","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#choosing-vector-index-type","content":"Use `HnswIndexParam()` to configure an HNSW index.","locale":"en"},"1770":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-38","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#choosing-vector-index-type","content":"Requires **Python SDK 0.8.1 or later**. This example creates an HNSW-PQ8 collection with OPQ at `./hnsw_pq`; use a new path. The highlighted lines enable PQ, configure its codebooks, and train the index.","locale":"en"},"1771":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-39","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#choosing-vector-index-type","content":"The synthetic vectors make this example self-contained; use representative embeddings in practice. After inserting data, `collection.optimize()` trains the codebooks and builds the PQ index. Before optimization, queries use the raw Flat index.","locale":"en"},"1772":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-40","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#choosing-vector-index-type","content":"Run the PQ query and refinement example next to search this collection. IVF-PQ4, FastScan, and parameter trade-offs are covered in Product Quantization.","locale":"en"},"1773":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-41","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#choosing-vector-index-type","content":"Use `HnswRabitqIndexParam()` to configure an HNSW-RaBitQ index.","locale":"en"},"1774":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-42","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#choosing-vector-index-type","content":"Use `IVFIndexParam()` to configure an IVF index.","locale":"en"},"1775":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-43","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#choosing-vector-index-type","content":"Use `IvfRabitqIndexParam()` to configure an IVF-RaBitQ index.","locale":"en"},"1776":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-44","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#choosing-vector-index-type","content":"Use `DiskAnnIndexParam()` to configure a DiskANN index.","locale":"en"},"1777":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema-45","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/create/schema#full-schema-example","content":"This example uses an inverted index and an HNSW index.","locale":"en"},"1778":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","type":"page","content":"DiskANN Index","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Introduction","Concepts","Vector Index"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","locale":"en"},"1779":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","content":"A disk-based graph index for billion-scale approximate nearest neighbor search, delivering high recall with a much smaller memory footprint at the cost of lower QPS.","locale":"en"},"1780":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#how-it-works","content":"How It Works","locale":"en"},"1781":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#when-to-use-a-diskann-index","content":"When to Use a DiskANN Index?","locale":"en"},"1782":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#advantages","content":"Advantages","locale":"en"},"1783":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#trade-offs","content":"Trade-offs","locale":"en"},"1784":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#key-parameters","content":"Key Parameters","locale":"en"},"1785":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#index-time-parameters","content":"Index-Time Parameters","locale":"en"},"1786":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#query-time-parameters","content":"Query-Time Parameters","locale":"en"},"1787":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","content":"A disk-based graph index designed for **billion-scale** vector search — keeping compressed vectors in memory and full-precision vectors on disk, enabling high-recall approximate nearest neighbor search with a **dramatically smaller memory footprint**.","locale":"en"},"1788":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","content":"DiskANN was introduced by Subramanya et al. in the NeurIPS 2019 paper DiskANN: Fast Accurate Billion-point Nearest Neighbor Search on a Single Node.","locale":"en"},"1789":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","content":"**`libaio` is optional.** When it is available, DiskANN uses Linux asynchronous I/O for better performance. Without `libaio`, DiskANN continues to work using a fallback I/O path, but queries may be slower.","locale":"en"},"1790":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","content":"The trade-off: because every query path involves disk I/O, DiskANN delivers **lower QPS than pure in-memory indexes** (such as HNSW). It is best suited for throughput- and latency-tolerant workloads that must handle very large datasets under tight memory budgets.","locale":"en"},"1791":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#how-it-works","content":"DiskANN builds a Vamana graph over the full dataset and stores it on disk along with the original vectors. At search time, only compressed PQ (Product Quantization) codes live in memory, while the graph and full-precision vectors are read from disk on demand.","locale":"en"},"1792":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#how-it-works","content":"**Vamana graph for navigation** 🪜","locale":"en"},"1793":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#how-it-works","content":"A single-layer graph where each node is connected to up to `max_degree` neighbors.","locale":"en"},"1794":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#how-it-works","content":"The graph is built using a greedy search-and-prune strategy with an **alpha parameter** that encourages long-range edges, providing fast convergence to the query's neighborhood.","locale":"en"},"1795":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#how-it-works","content":"A **medoid** (the point closest to the dataset's centroid) serves as the fixed entry point for every search.","locale":"en"},"1796":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#how-it-works","content":"**Product Quantization (PQ) for distance estimation** 🔍","locale":"en"},"1797":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#how-it-works","content":"The vector space is split into `pq_chunk_num` sub-spaces, and each sub-vector is quantized into a 256-centroid codebook (8-bit PQ codes).","locale":"en"},"1798":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#how-it-works","content":"At query time, a **PQ distance lookup table** is precomputed for the query, allowing approximate distances to all candidates to be computed via fast table lookups instead of full-precision arithmetic.","locale":"en"},"1799":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#how-it-works","content":"**Cached beam search** 🔎","locale":"en"},"1800":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#how-it-works","content":"Search starts from the medoid and explores the graph using a **beam search** strategy — multiple frontier nodes are expanded concurrently via batched disk I/O.","locale":"en"},"1801":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#how-it-works","content":"Frequently accessed nodes near the entry point are cached in memory (**BFS-level caching**), reducing disk reads for hot regions of the graph.","locale":"en"},"1802":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#how-it-works","content":"For each visited node, approximate distances are computed using PQ codes, and the full-precision vector is read from disk to compute the exact distance for the top-k result candidates.","locale":"en"},"1803":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#when-to-use-a-diskann-index","content":"✅ Billion-scale datasets that **cannot fit entirely in memory**","locale":"en"},"1804":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#when-to-use-a-diskann-index","content":"✅ Cost-sensitive deployments where minimizing RAM is critical","locale":"en"},"1805":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#when-to-use-a-diskann-index","content":"✅ Batch workloads and offline analytics that can tolerate slightly higher latency per query compared to in-memory indexes","locale":"en"},"1806":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#when-to-use-a-diskann-index","content":"**Best Practice**: Use DiskANN when your dataset far exceeds available RAM. It provides strong recall with memory consumption proportional only to PQ codes, not full vectors. For datasets that fit in memory, prefer HNSW or HNSW-RaBitQ for lower latency.","locale":"en"},"1807":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#advantages","content":"✨ **Extremely low memory footprint** — Only PQ-compressed codes (1 byte per chunk per vector) reside in memory, making billion-scale search feasible on commodity hardware","locale":"en"},"1808":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#advantages","content":"✨ **High recall** — The Vamana graph preserves connectivity and diversity through its alpha-based pruning, and exact distances are recomputed for final candidates","locale":"en"},"1809":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#advantages","content":"✨ **Scalable graph construction** — Built with a simple greedy insert-and-prune algorithm that can be parallelized across threads","locale":"en"},"1810":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-31","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#trade-offs","content":"⚠️ **Higher query latency** — Each search requires disk I/O for graph traversal, making it slower than pure in-memory indexes like HNSW","locale":"en"},"1811":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-32","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#trade-offs","content":"⚠️ **Build-time PQ training** — Requires a KMeans-based PQ training step before index construction, adding to the total build time","locale":"en"},"1812":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-33","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#trade-offs","content":"⚠️ **Not suited for real-time workloads** — Disk access latency means DiskANN is better for latency-tolerant use cases or scenarios with relatively low QPS requirements","locale":"en"},"1813":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-34","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#key-parameters","content":"**Tuning Tip**:\nStart with defaults. Adjust `list_size` at query time first for recall/latency trade-offs. Only increase `max_degree` if you need better recall — but expect higher disk usage and longer build times. Reduce `pq_chunk_num` if you need to cut memory further and can tolerate lower recall.","locale":"en"},"1814":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-35","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#index-time-parameters","content":"Parameter","locale":"en"},"1815":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-36","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#index-time-parameters","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"1816":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-37","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#index-time-parameters","content":"Tuning Guidance","locale":"en"},"1817":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-38","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#index-time-parameters","content":"`metric_type`","locale":"en"},"1818":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-39","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#index-time-parameters","content":"**Similarity metric** used to compare vectors","locale":"en"},"1819":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-40","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#index-time-parameters","content":"Choose based on how your embeddings were trained","locale":"en"},"1820":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-41","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#index-time-parameters","content":"`max_degree`","locale":"en"},"1821":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-42","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#index-time-parameters","content":"**Max neighbors per node** — The maximum number of edges per node in the Vamana graph","locale":"en"},"1822":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-43","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#index-time-parameters","content":"• Higher `max_degree` →  ✨ better recall and graph connectivity  ⚠️ more disk usage and longer build time","locale":"en"},"1823":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-44","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#index-time-parameters","content":"`list_size`","locale":"en"},"1824":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-45","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#index-time-parameters","content":"**Build-time candidate list size** — Number of candidates considered during graph construction when inserting a new vector","locale":"en"},"1825":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-46","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#index-time-parameters","content":"• Higher `list_size` →  ✨ better graph quality and higher recall  ⚠️ longer index build time","locale":"en"},"1826":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-47","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#index-time-parameters","content":"`pq_chunk_num`","locale":"en"},"1827":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-48","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#index-time-parameters","content":"**Number of PQ sub-spaces** — Controls how the vector dimensions are partitioned for Product Quantization","locale":"en"},"1828":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-49","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#index-time-parameters","content":"• More chunks →  ✨ finer-grained distance approximation and better recall  ⚠️ more memory for PQ codes (1 byte per chunk per vector)","locale":"en"},"1829":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-50","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index#query-time-parameters","content":"Parameter","locale":"en"},"1830":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index-51","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/diskann-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/conce