:"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites","locale":"en"},"2615":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"Performing Multi-Vector Search","locale":"en"},"2616":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Re-ranking Strategies","locale":"en"},"2617":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","content":"Zvec supports **multi-vector queries**, allowing you to combine different embeddings in a single search.","locale":"en"},"2618":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","content":"When querying multiple vector embeddings, Zvec retrieves candidates from each vector space independently and then fuses them into one relevance-ordered list. Because scores from different vector spaces might not be directly comparable, you must choose a suitable **re-ranking strategy**.","locale":"en"},"2619":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"This guide assumes:","locale":"en"},"2620":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"You have opened a `collection` with multiple vector fields","locale":"en"},"2621":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"You're familiar with the basic vector querying concepts. If not, please review the single-vector search guide","locale":"en"},"2622":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"This example collection contains two vector fields:","locale":"en"},"2623":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"**`dense_embedding`** — A 768-dimensional dense vector using inner product metric","locale":"en"},"2624":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"**`sparse_embedding`** — A sparse vector using inner product metric","locale":"en"},"2625":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"It also includes two scalar fields (`publish_year` and `category`).","locale":"en"},"2626":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"In Python, pass a list of query specifications to `query()` and provide a fusion strategy through `reranker`. In Node.js, pass the sub-queries to `multiQuerySync()` or `multiQuery()` and configure `rerank`.","locale":"en"},"2627":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"This example queries both `dense_embedding` and `sparse_embedding` and uses `WeightedReRanker` to combine their results. Weights are positional and must follow the same order as `queries`.","locale":"en"},"2628":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"`topk` always controls the number of **final documents** returned after fusion.","locale":"en"},"2629":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"Python does not currently expose a separate candidate-count option for each sub-query in `Collection.query()`.","locale":"en"},"2630":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"Node.js supports `numCandidates` on each sub-query. If omitted, its default is `max(topk, 10)`.","locale":"en"},"2631":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"`topn` is used only when calling a re-ranker's standalone `rerank()` method; it is not a constructor argument.","locale":"en"},"2632":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Zvec provides different re-ranking strategies to combine scores from multiple vector fields.","locale":"en"},"2633":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Re-ranker","locale":"en"},"2634":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"`WeightedReRanker`","locale":"en"},"2635":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"`RrfReRanker` (Reciprocal Rank Fusion)","locale":"en"},"2636":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Approach","locale":"en"},"2637":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Combines normalized similarity scores using **custom weights**","locale":"en"},"2638":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Fuses results based only on **ranking positions** — no scores needed  With a zero-based rank *r* (the first result is 0), the RRF score is: $\\text{RRF}(r) = \\frac{1}{k + r + 1}$","locale":"en"},"2639":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Best for","locale":"en"},"2640":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"• Scores are reasonably comparable across vector fields  • You know the relative importance of each embedding type","locale":"en"},"2641":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"• Scores come from different metrics or scales  • You prefer a simple, robust, tuning-free method","locale":"en"},"2642":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Parameters","locale":"en"},"2643":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"`weights`: An ordered list aligned with `queries`. Score normalization uses each queried field's schema.","locale":"en"},"2644":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"`rank_constant` (*k*): Controls how quickly rank influence decreases. Higher values reduce the dominance of top-ranked results.","locale":"en"},"2645":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"page","content":"Single Vector","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations","Query"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","locale":"en"},"2646":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites","locale":"en"},"2647":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"Performing Single-Vector Search","locale":"en"},"2648":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#parameters","content":"Parameters","locale":"en"},"2649":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#common-parameters","content":"Common Parameters","locale":"en"},"2650":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#index-specific-parameters","content":"Index-Specific Parameters","locale":"en"},"2651":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#query-refinement","content":"Query Refinement","locale":"en"},"2652":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","content":"Single-vector search finds documents most similar to a single query embedding. This is the most common search pattern in vector databases.","locale":"en"},"2653":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#prerequisites","content":"This guide assumes you have opened a collection and have a `collection` object ready.","locale":"en"},"2654":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#prerequisites","content":"This example collection contains two vector fields:","locale":"en"},"2655":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#prerequisites","content":"**`dense_embedding`** — A 768-dimensional dense vector using cosine metric","locale":"en"},"2656":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#prerequisites","content":"**`sparse_embedding`** — A sparse vector using inner product metric","locale":"en"},"2657":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#prerequisites","content":"It also includes two scalar fields (`publish_year` and `category`).","locale":"en"},"2658":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"To perform a single-vector similarity search, use the `query()` method and provide a single query specification.","locale":"en"},"2659":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"All queries return a `list[Doc]` containing the **top-k** most similar documents, sorted by relevance score.","locale":"en"},"2660":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"Each `Doc` object includes:","locale":"en"},"2661":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"`id`: The document identifier.","locale":"en"},"2662":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"`score`: The similarity score.","locale":"en"},"2663":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"`vectors`: A map from vector field names to their corresponding embedding values.\\\nThis is **only populated** if `include_vector=True` is passed in the query.","locale":"en"},"2664":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"`fields`: A map from scalar field names to their stored values.\\\nBy default, **all scalar fields** are returned; this can be restricted using the `output_fields` parameter.","locale":"en"},"2665":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"This example shows results from a query on the `dense_embedding` field with the following settings:","locale":"en"},"2666":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"`topk=3:` returns the 3 most similar documents","locale":"en"},"2667":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"`include_vector=False` (default): vector embeddings are not returned, so `vectors` is empty","locale":"en"},"2668":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"All scalar fields are returned","locale":"en"},"2669":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"Cosine distance is used to compute similarity scores — lower scores indicate greater similarity","locale":"en"},"2670":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#parameters","content":"When performing a vector search, the `query()` method accepts two kinds of parameters:","locale":"en"},"2671":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#parameters","content":"**common parameters**, which apply universally regardless of the underlying index type","locale":"en"},"2672":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#parameters","content":"**index-specific parameters**, which allow fine-tuning of search behavior based on the vector index in use","locale":"en"},"2673":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#common-parameters","content":"Parameter","locale":"en"},"2674":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#common-parameters","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"2675":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#common-parameters","content":"`topk`","locale":"en"},"2676":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#common-parameters","content":"The number of most similar documents to return.","locale":"en"},"2677":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-31","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#common-parameters","content":"`include_vector`","locale":"en"},"2678":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-32","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#common-parameters","content":"If `True`, the returned `Doc` objects include the full vector embeddings (disabled by default for performance).","locale":"en"},"2679":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-33","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#common-parameters","content":"`output_fields`","locale":"en"},"2680":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-34","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#common-parameters","content":"An optional list of scalar field names to include in results. If omitted, all scalar fields are returned.","locale":"en"},"2681":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-35","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#common-parameters","content":"`filter`","locale":"en"},"2682":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-36","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#common-parameters","content":"An optional SQL-like boolean expression to restrict results. See filtered search for details.","locale":"en"},"2683":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-37","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#common-parameters","content":"The `reranker` parameter is part of the `query()` interface but **only applies to multi-vector search**.\\\nDo not provide it in single-vector queries.","locale":"en"},"2684":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-38","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#index-specific-parameters","content":"You can fine-tune search behavior by passing index-specific query parameters through the `param` option in the `Query` object.","locale":"en"},"2685":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-39","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#index-specific-parameters","content":"The exact type and structure of these `param` depend on the vector index used for the target vector embedding. If omitted, default values are used.","locale":"en"},"2686":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-40","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#index-specific-parameters","content":"Each index type exposes its own set of tunable options at query time. For full details:","locale":"en"},"2687":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-41","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/que