s/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#index-specific-parameters","content":"If `dense_embedding` uses a DiskANN index, you can adjust the `list_size` parameter like this:","locale":"en"},"2698":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-52","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#query-refinement","content":"Refinement re-scores retrieved candidates using reference vectors, improving the ranking after approximate search. It is used by the HNSW-PQ8 example below and the IVF-RaBitQ example above.","locale":"en"},"2699":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-53","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#query-refinement","content":"`is_using_refiner=True` enables re-scoring of the candidate results.","locale":"en"},"2700":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-54","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#query-refinement","content":"`scale_factor` controls how many candidates enter refinement. With `topk=10` and `scale_factor=4`, the search requests approximately 40 candidates, then returns the best 10 after re-scoring. Increasing this value adds candidate-scoring work.","locale":"en"},"2701":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-55","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#query-refinement","content":"Requires **Python SDK 0.8.1 or later**. First run the HNSW-PQ8 creation example, then run this code from the same working directory. It opens `./hnsw_pq` and returns 10 refined results.","locale":"en"},"2702":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-56","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#query-refinement","content":"Tune `ef` together with `scale_factor` to balance recall and latency. Refinement only reorders retrieved candidates; it cannot recover missing neighbors. See Product Quantization for the trade-offs.","locale":"en"},"2703":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","type":"page","content":"Quantization","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Introduction","Concepts","Vector Index","Quantization"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","locale":"en"},"2704":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#storage-behavior","content":"Storage Behavior","locale":"en"},"2705":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#quantization-types","content":"Quantization Types","locale":"en"},"2706":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","content":"Quantization is a compression technique that &#x2A;**transforms vectors from their original (specifically FP32) format into a more compact representation***, reducing the size of vector indexes used for search.","locale":"en"},"2707":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","content":"This transformation approximates vectors using compact per-dimension or subvector encodings — enabling:","locale":"en"},"2708":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","content":"✨ Lower **memory footprint** — especially when the index is memory-resident,","locale":"en"},"2709":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","content":"✨ Faster I/O and lower query latency — due to reduced data movement and efficient integer/fp16 arithmetic,","locale":"en"},"2710":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","content":"✨ Better scalability on resource-constrained hardware.","locale":"en"},"2711":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","content":"**Important**:","locale":"en"},"2712":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","content":"Quantization is a &#x2A;**lossy and irreversible*** compression method. It improves runtime efficiency **at the cost of potentially reduced recall accuracy**. Always validate its effect on your retrieval quality.","locale":"en"},"2713":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","content":"Quantization only provides benefits when applied to vectors in a **FP32** format.","locale":"en"},"2714":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#storage-behavior","content":"To ensure data integrity and flexibility, **Zvec stores both the original vectors and their quantized versions**. This means:","locale":"en"},"2715":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#storage-behavior","content":"The **overall on-disk storage usage may increase** (due to storing two copies).","locale":"en"},"2716":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#storage-behavior","content":"**Quantized codes can reduce vector memory usage during search**. PQ training still requires original vectors, and query refinement reads reference vectors to re-score candidates.","locale":"en"},"2717":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#storage-behavior","content":"Users can always **retrieve the original, unaltered vectors** when needed.","locale":"en"},"2718":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#quantization-types","content":"Zvec provides two families of quantization. &#x2A;*Scalar Quantization (SQ)** encodes each dimension independently, while &#x2A;*Product Quantization (PQ)** jointly encodes groups of dimensions as subvectors.","locale":"en"},"2719":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#quantization-types","content":"Type","locale":"en"},"2720":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#quantization-types","content":"Representation","locale":"en"},"2721":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#quantization-types","content":"Configuration and Examples","locale":"en"},"2722":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#quantization-types","content":"Scalar Quantization (SQ)","locale":"en"},"2723":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#quantization-types","content":"Lower-precision values for each dimension","locale":"en"},"2724":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#quantization-types","content":"FP16, INT8, INT4, and optional random rotation","locale":"en"},"2725":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#quantization-types","content":"Product Quantization (PQ)","locale":"en"},"2726":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#quantization-types","content":"Subvector codes from trained codebooks","locale":"en"},"2727":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#quantization-types","content":"PQ4, PQ8, optional OPQ, and IVF-PQ4 FastScan","locale":"en"},"2728":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization#quantization-types","content":"Choose a quantization method based on your memory budget and retrieval-quality requirements, then measure recall and latency on representative data. See the pages above for configuration, SDK requirements, and examples.","locale":"en"},"2729":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","type":"page","content":"Product Quantization (PQ)","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Introduction","Concepts","Vector Index","Quantization"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","locale":"en"},"2730":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","content":"Configure PQ4, PQ8, OPQ, and IVF FastScan for HNSW and IVF indexes.","locale":"en"},"2731":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#code-size-and-accuracy","content":"Code Size and Accuracy","locale":"en"},"2732":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"Configuration","locale":"en"},"2733":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#fastscan-execution-paths","content":"FastScan Execution Paths","locale":"en"},"2734":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#training-and-lifecycle","content":"Training and Lifecycle","locale":"en"},"2735":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#query-and-refine-results","content":"Query and Refine Results","locale":"en"},"2736":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#enabling-quantization","content":"Enabling Quantization","locale":"en"},"2737":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#enabling-rotation","content":"Enabling Rotation","locale":"en"},"2738":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","content":"Product Quantization (PQ) splits each vector into `num_chunk` subvectors and represents each subvector with a code from a trained codebook. Unlike scalar quantization, which compresses individual dimensions, PQ compresses groups of dimensions.","locale":"en"},"2739":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","content":"Zvec supports PQ with **HNSW and IVF**, **dense FP32 vectors**, and **L2, IP, and COSINE** metrics.","locale":"en"},"2740":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","content":"Python supports HNSW/IVF PQ starting with **0.8.1**. **Node.js SDK 0.8.0** does not expose PQ configuration. The examples on this page use the Python API.","locale":"en"},"2741":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#code-size-and-accuracy","content":"Choose the **code width** first, then optional optimizations. These are separate configuration decisions, not four alternative quantization methods.","locale":"en"},"2742":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#code-size-and-accuracy","content":"**Choose PQ4 or PQ8** with `num_bits`: PQ4 uses 4 bits per subvector (16 codebook entries); PQ8 uses 8 bits (256 entries).","locale":"en"},"2743":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#code-size-and-accuracy","content":"**Optionally enable OPQ** with `enable_rotate=True`. Optimized Product Quantization learns a rotation to reduce quantization error and can be combined with either code width.","locale":"en"},"2744":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#code-size-and-accuracy","content":"**For IVF-PQ4, optionally enable FastScan** with `fast_scan=True` to scan packed codes. See the Faiss FastScan documentation for background on 4-bit codes and register-based lookup tables. In Zvec, this option requires IVF and `num_bits=4`; it does not apply to HNSW or PQ8.","locale":"en"},"2745":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#code-size-and-accuracy","content":"The code payload per vector is approximately `num_chunk × num_bits / 8` bytes. For example, a 768-dimensional FP32 vector occupies 3,072 bytes before compression; with 96 chunks, its PQ8 code occupies 96 bytes and its PQ4 code occupies 48 bytes. These figures exclude codebooks, index structures, metadata, and retained original vectors; they are **not total collection memory or disk sizes**.","locale":"en"},"2746":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#code-size-and-accuracy","content":"More chunks or more bits generally preserve more information at a higher storage and computation cost. Measure recall and latency on your own data when choosing a configuration.","locale":"en"},"2747":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"Parameter","locale":"en"},"2748":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"2749":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"Meaning and Constraints","locale":"en"},"2750":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"`num_chunk`","locale":"en"},"2751":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"`8`","locale":"en"},"2752":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"Number of subvectors. Must be positive and no greater than the vector dimension. With PQ4, the dimension must be divisible by this value.","locale":"en"},"2753":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"`num_bits`","locale":"en"},"2754":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"`8`","locale":"en"},"2755":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"Bits per subvector code: `4` or `8`.","locale":"en"},"2756":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"`enable_rotate`","locale":"en"},"2757":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"`False`","locale":"en"},"2758":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"Enables learned OPQ for PQ. This differs from the random rotation used by INT8/INT4 scalar quantization.","locale":"en"},"2759":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"`fast_scan`","locale":"en"},"2760":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"`False`","locale":"en"},"2761":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-31","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"Enables FastScan. Requires **IVF with PQ4**; HNSW and PQ8 do not support it.","locale":"en"},"2762":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-32","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"`opq_iter`","locale":"en"},"2763":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-33","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"`5`","locale":"en"},"2764":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-34","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"OPQ training iterations. Must be positive when OPQ is enabled.","locale":"en"},"2765":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-35","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"`opq_pq_iter`","locale":"en"},"2766":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-36","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"`4`","locale":"en"},"2767":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-37","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"PQ training iterations within each OPQ iteration. Must be positive when OPQ is enabled.","locale":"en"},"2768":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-38","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#configuration","content":"For IVF-PQ4 FastScan, use `IVFIndexParam` with `quantize_type=QuantizeType.PQ` and `QuantizerParam(num_chunk=16, num_bits=4, fast_scan=True)` for a 128-dimensional field. Add `enable_rotate=True` only if OPQ is desired. See the platform matrix for per-platform availability.","locale":"en"},"2769":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-39","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#fastscan-execution-paths","content":"**Feature availability and SIMD acceleration are distinct.** FastScan is available only with IVF-PQ4. The v0.8.1 kernel dispatcher selects an implementation based on CPU capabilities:","locale":"en"},"2770":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-40","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#fastscan-execution-paths","content":"CPU Capabilities","locale":"en"},"2771":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-41","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#fastscan-execution-paths","content":"FastScan Execution Path","locale":"en"},"2772":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-42","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#fastscan-execution-paths","content":"x86\\_64 with AVX512F and AVX512BW","locale":"en"},"2773":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-43","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#fastscan-execution-paths","content":"AVX-512","locale":"en"},"2774":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-44","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#fastscan-execution-paths","content":"x86\\_64 with AVX2","locale":"en"},"2775":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-45","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#fastscan-execution-paths","content":"AVX2","locale":"en"},"2776":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-46","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#fastscan-execution-paths","content":"ARM64 with NEON","locale":"en"},"2777":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-47","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#fastscan-execution-paths","content":"NEON","locale":"en"},"2778":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-48","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#fastscan-execution-paths","content":"No matching SIMD path","locale":"en"},"2779":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-49","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#fastscan-execution-paths","content":"Scalar fallback","locale":"en"},"2780":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-50","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#fastscan-execution-paths","content":"The build must also include the relevant SIMD implementation. Missing a listed instruction set does not by itself make PQ or FastScan unavailable: the implementation provides a scalar fallback. Scalar fallback does not imply equal performance across CPUs.","locale":"en"},"2781":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-51","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#training-and-lifecycle","content":"PQ training runs during `Collection.optimize()`. Before optimization, untrained data remains searchable through the raw Flat index. Insert representative data before optimizing; creating a PQ schema alone does not build a trained compressed index.","locale":"en"},"2782":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-52","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#training-and-lifecycle","content":"Trained codebooks and quantizer settings persist when the collection is closed and reopened. Writable collections also support subsequent updates; optimization can train and rebuild indexes as data changes.","locale":"en"},"2783":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-53","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#training-and-lifecycle","content":"To use ordinary IVF-PQ4, set `fast_scan=False`; to use IVF-PQ8, also set `num_bits=8`.","locale":"en"},"2784":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-54","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#query-and-refine-results","content":"PQ search uses approximate distances. Enable `is_using_refiner` to re-score candidates using the reference vectors. `scale_factor` controls candidate expansion: a value of 4 requests approximately four times `topk` candidates before refinement.","locale":"en"},"2785":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-55","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#query-and-refine-results","content":"Refinement adds reference-vector reads and scoring work. It improves ranking within the retrieved candidate set but cannot recover neighbors that were never retrieved. Tune HNSW `ef` or IVF `nprobe` together with `scale_factor`, measuring recall and latency.","locale":"en"},"2786":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-56","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#query-and-refine-results","content":"See HNSW, IVF, and collection optimization for the surrounding index lifecycle.","locale":"en"},"2787":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-57","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#enabling-quantization","content":"In the `HnswIndexParam` or `IVFIndexParam` passed to `VectorSchema.index_param&#x60;, set &#x2A;*`quantize_type=zvec.QuantizeType.PQ`** and pass a `zvec.QuantizerParam` through `quantizer_param` to configure PQ.","locale":"en"},"2788":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-58","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#enabling-quantization","content":"After configuring the schema, insert representative data and call `collection.optimize()` to train the codebooks and build the PQ index. Queries before optimization use the original Flat index. See the HNSW-PQ8 creation example for the complete workflow.","locale":"en"},"2789":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-59","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#enabling-rotation","content":"When using PQ, set &#x2A;*`enable_rotate=True`** in the index parameters' `quantizer_param` to enable &#x2A;*Optimized Product Quantization (OPQ)**. OPQ learns a rotation from the training data to reduce quantization error; INT8/INT4 scalar quantization uses a random orthogonal rotation. This option defaults to `False`, works with PQ4 or PQ8, and can be enabled independently of IVF-PQ4 FastScan.","locale":"en"},"2790":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization-60","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/product-quantization#enabling-rotation","content":"After inserting representative data, call `collection.optimize()` to run training. OPQ adds training work; `opq_iter` and `opq_pq_iter` control the iteration counts. Measure recall and training time on your own data when evaluating OPQ.","locale":"en"},"2791":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","type":"page","content":"Scalar Quantization (SQ)","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Introduction","Concepts","Vector Index","Quantization"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","locale":"en"},"2792":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","content":"Configure FP16, INT8, INT4, and random rotation for scalar quantization.","locale":"en"},"2793":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization#quantization-types","content":"Quantization Types","locale":"en"},"2794":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization#fp16-half-precision-floating-point","content":"FP16 (Half-Precision Floating Point)","locale":"en"},"2795":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization#int8-8-bit-integer-quantization","content":"INT8 (8-Bit Integer Quantization)","locale":"en"},"2796":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization#int4-4-bit-integer-quantization","content":"INT4 (4-Bit Integer Quantization)","locale":"en"},"2797":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization#enabling-quantization","content":"Enabling Quantization","locale":"en"},"2798":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization#enabling-rotation","content":"Enabling Rotation","locale":"en"},"2799":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","content":"Scalar Quantization (SQ) reduces the precision of each vector dimension independently. FP16 uses a smaller floating-point representation, while INT8 and INT4 use integer quantization. Unlike Product Quantization (PQ), SQ encodes individual dimensions rather than groups of dimensions.","locale":"en"},"2800":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization#fp16-half-precision-floating-point","content":"Converts FP32 source vectors to 16-bit floating-point values, reducing the size of the vector representation at the cost of lower numerical precision. Measure recall and latency on your own data to assess whether FP16 meets your retrieval-quality requirements.","locale":"en"},"2801":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization#int8-8-bit-integer-quantization","content":"Converts FP32 source vectors to 8-bit integer values, reducing the size of the vector representation and memory bandwidth requirements. Quantization introduces approximation error; evaluate recall and latency when choosing INT8.","locale":"en"},"2802":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization#int4-4-bit-integer-quantization","content":"Converts FP32 source vectors to 4-bit integer values. INT4 uses fewer bits per dimension than INT8, but may introduce more quantization error. Consider it when memory is constrained, and validate its effect on recall and latency.","locale":"en"},"2803":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization#enabling-quantization","content":"Set `quantize_type` to `FP16`, `INT8`, or `INT4` in the index parameters passed to `VectorSchema.index_param`, such as `HnswIndexParam` or `IVFIndexParam`. SQ is the name of this quantization family; the API uses the individual type names.","locale":"en"},"2804":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization#enabling-quantization","content":"See the HNSW schema example for an INT8 configuration. Zvec manages the quantized representation alongside the original vectors; see Storage Behavior for the storage and memory trade-offs.","locale":"en"},"2805":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-index/quantization/scalar-quantization#enabling-rotation","content":"When using `INT8` or `INT4` quantization, you can **set `enable_rotate=True` via the `quantizer_param` parameter in your index parameters** to enable rotation. This applies a random orthogonal rotation before quantization to distribute vector values more evenly across dimensions. It can reduce quantization error; measure the effect on recall with your own data. For PQ, this option enables learned OPQ instead.","locale":"en"},"2806":{"id":"/zh/docs","page_id":"/zh/docs","type":"page","content":"总览","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/zh/docs","locale":"zh"},"2807":{"id":"/zh/docs-0","page_id":"/zh/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh/docs","content":"对比两个产品，选择合适的起点。","locale":"zh"},"2808":{"id":"/zh/docs/db/ai-friendly","page_id":"/zh/docs/db/ai-friendly","type":"page","content":"AI 友好","breadcrumbs":["Docs","产品","Zvec","使用指南"],"tags":[],"url":"/zh/docs/db/ai-friendly","locale":"zh"},"2809":{"id":"/zh/docs/db/ai-friendly-0","page_id":"/zh/docs/db/ai-friendly","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/zh/docs/db/ai-friendly#快速开始复制-prompt","content":"快速开始：复制 Prompt","locale":"zh"},"2810":{"id":"/zh/docs/db/ai-friendly-1","page_id":"/zh/docs/db/ai-friendly","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/zh/docs/db/ai-friendly#复制页面按钮","content":"复制页面按钮","locale":"zh"},"2811":{"id":"/zh/docs/db/ai-friendly-2","page_id":"/zh/docs/db/ai-friendly","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/zh/docs/db/ai-friendly#可用端点","content":"可用端点","locale":"zh"},"2812":{"id":"/zh/docs/db/ai-friendly-3","page_id":"/zh/docs/db/ai-friendly","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh/docs/db/ai